You are an expert in React, TypeScript, Python, FastAPI, Weaviate v4, Tavus CVI, and kiosk application development, with deep understanding of accessibility, real-time systems, and conference management platforms.

## Project Context
- **Rosa Kiosk**: AI-powered voice-controlled kiosk for CTBTO SnT2025 conference
- **Target Environment**: Physical kiosk displays (not mobile), 85%/15% split-screen layout
- **Voice-First**: Designed for voice-only interaction with visual feedback
- **Real Conference Data**: Uses actual SnT2025 speaker profiles, sessions, and venue information

## Core Technologies
- **Frontend**: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Bun package manager
- **Backend**: Python 3.13, FastAPI, Weaviate v4, OpenAI API (GPT-4.1 family)
- **Video Interface**: Tavus CVI (Conversational Video Interface) with @daily-co integration
- **UI Library**: Radix UI primitives + Tailwind CSS (shadcn/ui patterns)
- **State Management**: Jotai for client state, 2-second polling for real-time updates
- **Animation**: Framer Motion (sparingly), respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Code Style and Architecture

### React Patterns
- Use functional components with hooks; avoid class components
- Separate logic (Handler components) from UI (Card components) 
- Follow compound component pattern for complex UI (Card.Title, Card.Body, etc.)
- Use TypeScript interfaces over types; prefer interfaces for extensibility
- Implement proper error boundaries and loading states

### Component Architecture
- **Handlers**: Data fetching, polling, business logic (e.g., SessionHandler, SpeakerHandler)
- **Cards**: Pure presentational components with props interface
- **Compound Components**: Flexible composition (Card.Image, Card.Actions)
- Single responsibility principle: one component, one job

### Async Patterns
- **Backend**: Fire-and-forget using `asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe()`
- **Frontend**: 2-second polling intervals for real-time updates
- Store results immediately, process in background
- Never await long-running operations in API response handlers

### State Management
- Use session-based data storage for multi-user kiosk scenarios
- Check connection state before polling
- Implement graceful error handling without breaking main flow
- No WebSockets - polling works better for this use case

## Accessibility & Kiosk-Specific Requirements

### WCAG AAA Compliance
- Minimum 7:1 contrast ratio (#1a1a1a on white)
- Minimum 18px font size for standing users
- Large touch targets (44px minimum)
- Semantic HTML with proper ARIA labels
- Screen reader compatibility

### Kiosk UX Patterns
- Fixed positioning for persistent UI elements
- Reserve bottom 15vh for sticky interface
- Prevent content overflow with `overflow: hidden`
- No hover states as primary interaction method
- No close buttons (voice-controlled)
- No scrollable content in kiosk mode

## Performance Optimization
- Tree-shake unused code; measure bundle impact of dependencies
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Dynamic imports for code splitting
- Optimize images for kiosk display resolution
- Debounce rapid state updates
- Leverage Web Vitals optimization (LCP, CLS, FID)

## Data Integration
- **Real Data Only**: Use actual SnT2025 speaker profiles, session titles, room names
- No placeholder data like "Dr. Smith" - reference actual conference data
- Integrate with Weaviate v4 knowledge graph (Speaker, Session, Topic, Room entities)
- Follow RAG patterns from `design-patterns/WEAVIATE/` directory

## Naming Conventions
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (isLoading, hasError)
- Lowercase with dashes for directories (components/auth-wizard)
- Favor named exports for functions
- Group related files by feature, not by type

## Key Conventions
- Always use Bun instead of npm for package management
- Place test files in root `tests/` directory (tests/frontend/, tests/backend/)
- Follow the established polling intervals (2-second) without modification
- Respect the fire-and-forget async pattern for backend operations
- Maintain the Handler/Card separation for component architecture
- Use compound components over boolean props for flexibility

## Environment & Deployment
- Frontend runs on port 5173 (Vite)
- Backend runs on port 8000 (FastAPI)
- Use environment variables for API keys and configuration
- Validate required environment variables at startup
- Never commit sensitive environment files

Focus on creating accessible, performant kiosk interfaces that work seamlessly with voice interaction and provide real-time conference information to SnT2025 attendees.

